 ### Surface Descendant Check
-An optimization for isosurface extraction where the traversal checks if a node or its descendants contain a sign change in the scalar field. If a node is a leaf, it returns whether it has a sign change. If it is a branch, it recursively checks its children. If empty or full, it returns false, allowing the traversal to skip the entire subtree [S4, unofficial].
+An optimization for isosurface extraction where the traversal checks if a node or its descendants contain a sign change in the scalar field [S4, unofficial]. If the cell is a leaf, it returns whether it has a sign change. If it is a branch, it recursively checks if any of its children have a surface descendant. If it is empty or full, it returns false, allowing the traversal to skip the entire subtree [S4, unofficial].
 
 ### Warp-Level Intersection Caching
-A GPU optimization that delays intersection tests until enough threads in a warp have stored an intersection child node. When an intersection is found, the voxel data is stored. At the start of each step, the warp checks if enough threads have stored intersections; if so, they proceed with the test. Otherwise, the warp continues traversing together. Threads that find a new intersection while already holding one stop until the next test phase [S8, unofficial].
+A GPU optimization that delays intersection tests until enough threads in a warp have stored an intersection child node [S8, unofficial]. When an intersection is found, the voxel intersection data is stored. At the start of every traversal step, the warp checks if enough threads have a stored intersection; if so, they proceed with the test. Otherwise, the warp continues traversing together. Threads that find the next intersection test while already having an intersection stored stop traversing until the next intersection test is performed [S8, unofficial].
 
 ### Packet Ray Traversal / Ray Coherence Optimization
-Configures CUDA grids/blocks as 2D to map spatially coherent threads (rays) to neighboring threads. This causes rays with similar directions to traverse the octree similarly, improving cache hit rates. A pitfall is thread divergence in deep subdivisions, causing SIMD stalls [S9, unofficial].
+Configures CUDA grids and block dimensions as 2D to map threads such that neighboring threads (rays) are spatially coherent (similar direction), causing them to traverse the octree in similar ways and improving cache hit rates [S9, unofficial]. A known pitfall is thread divergence in deep octree subdivisions, causing SIMD stalls on GPU architecture [S9, unofficial].
 
 ### Octree Traversal with Texture Memory Access
-Binds octree node data to CUDA texture objects and accesses them via `tex1Dfetch()`. This utilizes the texture cache for the random access patterns typical in tree traversal, preferred over constant memory due to size limits and broadcast optimization mismatches [S9, unofficial].
+Binds octree node data to a CUDA texture object and accesses node data using the `tex1Dfetch()` function, which utilizes the texture cache for random access patterns typical in tree traversal [S9, unofficial]. Texture memory is preferred over constant memory because constant memory is limited in size and optimized for broadcast reads, whereas octree traversal involves random access patterns across different nodes [S9, unofficial].
 
 ### Bookkeeping Method
-Inspired by Frisken & Perry (2002), this method avoids starting the search from the root node for every wall passage in simulations. It maintains bookkeeping state to continue traversal from the last known position, reducing overhead compared to top-down searches [S10].
+An octree traversal method inspired by Frisken & Perry (2002), designed to avoid starting the search from the root node for every wall passage [S10]. Unlike the top-down method, it does not require starting the search from the root node for every passage through a wall, reducing computational overhead [S10].
 
